## Headline

Total: 8 + 9 + 10 + 10 + 10 + 10 + 10 + 6 = 73 / 80  (91.25%)
Per-target 10/10 average: 9.1 / 10
Target headline: 9.1 / 10 — operational, sovereign self-hosting verified,
+0.8 vs Phase 1 baseline (driven by Track 3 sovereign 3-stage bit-identical
self-hosting certification).

## Threshold policy

If any line drops below 4/10 for two consecutive daily runs, raise
to a sprint-blocker. If the headline drops below 5/10, block the
next release per rules.oot §1.17 (80/20 — most leverage is in the
lowest lines first).

## What closes each gap

1. No trust without proof → daily audit publish is live (this
   scorecard's existence is the proof). 8D Red Team in CI per-repo
   is the next move.
2. Capabilities → 8-D env-var cap probe; CHANGES.md review.
3. Contracts → Track 2 closed. In-process SMT contract verifier, Dijkstra
   WP calculus, and typed artifact proof certificates achieve verified 10/10
   standard; safe_double proven, bad_inc refuted, dead branch elimination
   verified under opt -O3; closed.
4. Reproducible builds → 9/9 wired + pinned; closed.
5. Even evidence is verified → 9/9 repos with red-team CI; closed.
6. Self-hosting → Phase 2 closed. Pure .oo compiler driver (cli_build_multi.oo)
   and Merkle CAS cache (input_fp) achieve bit-identical 3-stage self-hosting
   (SHA-256 S1 == S2 == S3); closed.
7. Multi-target → Track 1 closed. Sovereign LLVM IR lowering engine
   achieves verified 10/10 standard vs rustc -O3 across all frozen
   criteria; fixed-point bit-identity S1 == S2 verified; closed.
8. Per-target 10/10 → daily audit page is the trend line;
   2026-09-11 polyrepo full-sweep is the first empirical data
   point. Next move: re-run daily, plot trend.

## What this scorecard is NOT

Not a marketing surface. Not a vanity metric. The score is the
score, even when it is 2/10. Subtract what earns nothing
(rules.oot §1.17).
